WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.534
-Guys, we have exactly
seven shows left

00:00:02.534 --> 00:00:04.200
before we go on Christmas break,
which means it's time

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:06.200
for that beloved
"Tonight Show" tradition.

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:09.334
It's time for
"12 Days of Christmas Sweaters."

00:00:09.334 --> 00:00:10.567
Here we go.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:10.567 --> 00:00:12.701
-♪ 12 Days
of Christmas Sweaters ♪

00:00:12.701 --> 00:00:17.767
♪ 7 days left ♪

00:00:17.767 --> 00:00:19.901
-That's right.
Every show between

00:00:19.901 --> 00:00:21.300
now and Christmas,
we'll be giving

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:24.901
one lucky audience member
an iconic Christmas sweater

00:00:24.901 --> 00:00:26.834
from the "Countdown
to Christmas" cabinet.

00:00:26.834 --> 00:00:32.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:32.601 --> 00:00:35.067
I'm not saying
it's worth $40,000,

00:00:35.067 --> 00:00:37.467
but it's pretty awesome.

00:00:37.467 --> 00:00:38.868
Since there
are seven shows left,

00:00:38.868 --> 00:00:42.133
let's open door number 7.

00:00:42.133 --> 00:00:43.801
You ready for this, pal?
-I'm ready.

00:00:43.801 --> 00:00:44.968
-Let's do it.

00:00:44.968 --> 00:00:46.734
[ Drum roll ]

00:00:46.734 --> 00:00:48.334
Oh, no, wow!
-Oh!

00:00:48.334 --> 00:00:50.067
♪♪

00:00:50.067 --> 00:00:52.567
[ Cheers and applause,
audience groans ]

00:00:52.567 --> 00:00:55.667
[ Band plays off-key ]

00:00:55.667 --> 00:00:57.667
[ Audience groans ]

00:00:57.667 --> 00:01:04.601
♪♪

00:01:04.601 --> 00:01:06.400
Uh, wow.

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:08.100
That's beautiful, that one.
Uh...

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:09.801
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.801 --> 00:01:11.067
Is there something on the back?

00:01:11.067 --> 00:01:12.834
-Oh, yeah.
-Oh, another one.

00:01:12.834 --> 00:01:14.033
Another little
scary something --

00:01:14.033 --> 00:01:16.634
[ Cheers and applause ]
At least he's happy.

00:01:16.634 --> 00:01:17.968
All right, at least he's happy.

00:01:17.968 --> 00:01:19.901
[ Applause ]

00:01:19.901 --> 00:01:21.367
Now let's see who's going home
with tonight's sweater.

00:01:21.367 --> 00:01:22.534
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.534 --> 00:01:24.667
You have to take the sweater
if you get it.

00:01:24.667 --> 00:01:25.801
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.801 --> 00:01:27.534
Everyone, look at
your seat number, please.

00:01:27.534 --> 00:01:30.100
If I call your number,
come on down.

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:32.133
Quest, can I get a drum roll,
please?

00:01:32.133 --> 00:01:35.968
[ Drum roll ]

00:01:35.968 --> 00:01:38.767
Here we go.

00:01:38.767 --> 00:01:41.234
Seat number 126.

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:43.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:43.868 --> 00:01:45.267
There you go!
Come on down!

00:01:45.267 --> 00:01:54.067
♪♪

00:01:54.067 --> 00:01:56.000
Hi! Welcome!

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:59.501
Thank you very much
for being here.

00:01:59.501 --> 00:02:02.167
Seat number 126.

00:02:02.167 --> 00:02:04.400
What is your name?
-I'm Ali.

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:05.667
-Ali, where are you from?

00:02:05.667 --> 00:02:08.434
-I'm from Virginia,
but I live in New York now.

00:02:08.434 --> 00:02:10.033
-Oh, you're in New York
right now.

00:02:10.033 --> 00:02:12.000
[ Cheers and applause ]
Well, today --

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:13.834
today, especially,
it got really cold out.

00:02:13.834 --> 00:02:16.300
I thought it felt very wintry.

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:18.200
You don't have anything
like that at home, do you?

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:20.033
-No.
This is my first one of these.

00:02:20.033 --> 00:02:21.300
-Yeah.
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:22.834
Here's the good news --
it goes with everything.

00:02:22.834 --> 00:02:24.267
-Oh, yes.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.267 --> 00:02:26.467
-Would you like to try it on?
-I would love to try it on.

00:02:26.467 --> 00:02:27.701
-Yeah, I'm sure.
Roots, can we just --

00:02:27.701 --> 00:02:29.334
I think it'll be perfect.

00:02:29.334 --> 00:02:30.534
Yeah, you throw it on your --
-Are you good?

00:02:30.534 --> 00:02:32.667
-Yeah.
There's no wrong way to wear it.

00:02:32.667 --> 00:02:34.334
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.334 --> 00:02:36.200
I'm not sure
if there's a right way, either.

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:38.267
-This is good.
-Oh, I can --

00:02:38.267 --> 00:02:41.467
I can already feel
this is gonna work out.

00:02:41.467 --> 00:02:42.901
Wait.
You make it look -- hey!

00:02:42.901 --> 00:02:44.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:44.367 --> 00:02:45.968
You make it look pretty good.

00:02:45.968 --> 00:02:48.834
Yeah, that's what
I'm talking about, Ali!

00:02:48.834 --> 00:02:50.767
You make it look great, buddy!
I love it!

00:02:50.767 --> 00:02:52.434
-Thank you!
-Congratulations once again

00:02:52.434 --> 00:02:54.000
to our winner.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:56.200
Stick around.
We're playing "True Confessions"

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:58.367
with Miley Cyrus
and Pete Davidson

00:02:58.367 --> 00:02:59.901
after the break.
Come on back.

00:02:59.901 --> 00:03:01.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:01.734 --> 00:03:10.801
♪♪

